WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.190
Achill Island, County Mayo,
off the west coast of Ireland.

2
00:00:04.240 --> 00:00:09.490
In 1911, the census
counted 5,260 people here.

3
00:00:09.540 --> 00:00:13.910
By 2022, just 2,345.

4
00:00:13.960 --> 00:00:18.990
On nearby Inis Bigil, 162 people in 1926.

5
00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:21.730
Just 25 in 2011.

6
00:00:21.780 --> 00:00:25.470
An island that lost over
half its people in a century.

7
00:00:25.520 --> 00:00:27.490
What happens to those who stay?

8
00:00:27.540 --> 00:00:30.110
In this mission, you'll
look behind the total,

9
00:00:30.160 --> 00:00:32.770
using Achill's own census data.

10
00:00:32.820 --> 00:00:36.550
Then you'll trace what a shrinking
population means for services,

11
00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:38.610
work and community life.

12
00:00:38.660 --> 00:00:43.550
Your mission: find out what out-migration
means for the people who stay on Achill.
